Firmware: ODROID-C5 bootloader: Amlogic's boot stages (BL2 and the stages it loads,
          BL30, BL31 and BL32, with their signed headers) and Hardkernel's U-Boot (BL33)
Hardware: Hardkernel ODROID-C5 (Amlogic S905X5M, SoC family S7D) only
Files:    the SD card's bootloader area: the MBR's boot code and the sectors from 1
          up to the first partition (at most 8 MiB); this file on the SD card's boot
          partition as /BOOTLOADER.txt
Source:   This notice is for a card made with ODROID_C5_BOOTLOADER_FROM; a card
          made with the firmware package amlogic-s7d-bootloader carries that
          package's notice instead.  Here the area is not fetched by zedBSD: it
          is copied, byte for byte, from the card image named by
          ODROID_C5_BOOTLOADER_FROM, which is expected to be one of Hardkernel's
          own ODROID-C5 operating system images (uncompressed; its first 8 MiB
          are enough), obtained by whoever builds the image.  The lines after
          "Copied from" on the card's copy name that image and the SHA-256 of
          the area taken from it.
          A donor known to work with this notice: Hardkernel's official image
          ubuntu-22.04-gnome-desktop-odroidc5-20260610-bsp-boot.img.xz
          (37760380 bytes, SHA-256
          04b9817d4e5e27ac4cc46dc4ad48fbc164e9a6c6f42eb1b0ba8d7a927accc5f2),
          the one the package uses; its MBR's boot code is zero, its
          bootloader is in sectors 1 to 6538 (the BL30 names itself
          S7D-s905x5m-26052812), and its sectors 1 to 16383 have the SHA-256
          b6a4b424f0a6dac33be4287d2bad6f2651466d983ca9e4146a29357b8e3c8cba.

Copyright (C) 2018 Amlogic, Inc. (the boot stages BL2 to BL32)
Copyright the U-Boot authors and Hardkernel Co., Ltd. (U-Boot)

Terms:
- Amlogic's boot stages are under Amlogic's license (the package's
  LICENSE.amlogic, in the zedBSD firmware repository's amlogic-s7d/): they
  are provided under a Software License Agreement with Amlogic, and
  redistribution and use without Amlogic's prior written permission are
  prohibited.  Amlogic has given that permission to Hardkernel, which
  distributes them in its images for the ODROID-C5, and such an image,
  which can be used only on this board, may be redistributed.  So use them
  only on a Hardkernel ODROID-C5, and pass on a card image made with
  ODROID_C5_BOOTLOADER_FROM only with that license and this notice, and
  only for use on the ODROID-C5.  A card image made with
  ODROID_C5_NO_BOOTLOADER=y carries none of them.
- U-Boot is GPL-2.0-or-later.  Its corresponding source is Hardkernel's: the
  submodule bl33/v2023 of the branch odroidc5-v2023.01 of
  https://github.com/hardkernel/u-boot (commit
  c99f3409d5cad031b365fd871e543f97af893f88), on
  https://git.odroid.com/yocto/uboot.  zedBSD changes nothing in it.
- The boot ROM accepts only stages signed for the S905X5M, so the area is used
  as it is; zedBSD does not modify, re-sign or rebuild it.
